    description: "FOUND 2026-09-24 while working WI-tisom (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tisom_09242026/).\n\nTHE DEFECT: the C# analyzer emits NO call edge for a call made inside a property accessor: `get { return Helper(); }`, `set { Helper(); }`, and expression-bodied `public int Twice => Helper() * 2;`. In the same fixture, the same call from a method emits `A.Run -> A.Helper`. The property symbols exist (kind=property, spans cover the bodies); nothing is credited to them and nothing is emitted.\n\nMEASURED: on sherpa-onnx, grpc, rabbitmq and microservices-demo, analyze_csharp emits 201 property symbols, 142 of which span more than one line. There are 0 edges from any of them and 1 edge to one.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: every call made in a C# getter or setter is missing from the call graph. The callee can read as dead, and a slice through the property is empty. WI-tisom stops the noise filter dropping C# properties, but they will carry no call edges until this is fixed.\n\nASKED: credit accessor calls to the property symbol, with the position-keyed enclosing lookup (INV-midag), and add csharp property accessors to the call-anchor gate fixture."  # 1feb
    fields: {}  # 1feb
